  "note": "The literal bin-count reading is contradicted where it is testable: at 322.41 nm three grid nodes lie in [wl, wl+5) so a bin sum predicts 3.00, while the measured value is 2.504 and 5/step gives 2.857; at 326.41 nm two nodes predict 2.00 against 2.500 measured; at 318.91 and 319.91 nm only four nodes lie in the window yet the measured value is 5.01; and the exact 1 nm step plateau rows measure 5.0016 where the node count gives 5, but the exact 2 nm rows measure 4.9991 where the node count in a 5 nm window gives 3 (2.5 in units of 2 nm).  The 1/step WIDTH ratio tracks all of these; the node count does not (mean |rel| 0.1738 vs 0.0046).",
